{"id": "q0032", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1851623335, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "It takes John 5 minutes to get to the first side of the Rubik's cube.  The second and third sides each take twice that long.  The last 2 sides each take half as long as the first, and once you get the 5th side you have all 6 sides.  How long does the Rubik's cube take?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0032.wav", "input_sha256": "dd6bb8eaf3ba4d96a20484261431d205031c7d63946e979d8a2fd7d9fc942c2e", "input_samples": 330400, "input_s": 20.65, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.2527, "act": 0.9994, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So the first side takes 5 minutes. The second and third sides each take twice that, so 10 minutes each. That gives us 20 minutes for those two. The last two sides take half as long as the first, so 2. 5 minutes each. Add ing all of that together: 5 + 1 0 + 10 + 2. 5 + 2. 5 equals 3 0 minutes total. So it takes 3 0 minutes to solve the cube.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 21, "feed_lag_max_ms": 7870, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 83173, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0032_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "ad6b01a813805182398d2b89cd58ba836c0d6a762cb58577665c35d731626b3b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 21.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.128, 1.232, 1, 0, 0