{"id": "q0046", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 644994425, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "Tim wanted to make lemonade for a pool party.  For a gallon of lemonade, his recipe called for 1 cup of fresh lemon juice.  He found that 6 lemons would yield 1 cup of juice.  He figured he would need to make 4 gallons of lemonade for the party.  His best friend Allen asked if Tim could make an extra gallon for him that was twice as tart as the other gallons.  How many lemons will Tim need?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0046.wav", "input_sha256": "32303a4d2647ea70e6aa653b6863131143cb196357ca08a522c9ca79b95a6459", "input_samples": 453200, "input_s": 28.325, "n_real_chunks": 29, "score": 0.4666, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So, Tim wants to make 4 gal lons of lemonade. Each gal lon requires 1 cup of lemon juice, so for 4 gal lons, he needs 4 cups of lemon juice. But Alan wants an extra gallon that's twice as tart, meaning it needs twice the lemon juice— so 2 cup s for that one gallon. That means total lemon juice needed is 4 plus 2, which is 6 cups. Since 6 lemons make 1 cup of juice, for 6 cups, he will need 6 times 6, which is 3 6 lemons. So, Tim will need 3 6 lemons.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 28, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 31, "feed_lag_max_ms": 15917, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 328019, "audio_files":