{"id": "q0068", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 4093614844, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "In a family, there are 2 brothers and 3 sisters. All sisters are the same age, which is 16. One of the brothers is 12 years old, which is half the age of the older brother. What is the total age of all these siblings?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0068.wav", "input_sha256": "ec3173c9c40b131f065591b344ef6b49756d2d167f3d63288d359278d48b5179", "input_samples": 284400, "input_s": 17.775, "n_real_chunks": 18, "score": 0.2443, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "All right, so there's two brothers and three sisters. The sisters are all 16 years old. So that means the total age of the sister s is 3 times 16, which is 4 8. Now, one brother is 1 2 years old, and that' s half the age of the older brother. So if one brother is 12, the other must be twice that, which is 24. So the total age for the brothers is 1 2 plus 24, which is 3 6. Add the sisters' age to the brothers', 4 8 plus 36, equals 8 4. So the total age of all the siblings is 8 4.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 38, "feed_lag_max_ms": 11253, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 206134, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0068_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "3938a373bfe81216a755ab11ca0b6b8ec2fb6ac2f2bd08e087be