{"id": "q0115", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3284998833, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "In the land of Ink, the money system is unique. One Trinket is equal to 4 Blinkets, and 3 Blinkets are equal to 7 Drinkets. In Trinkets, what is the value of 56 Drinkets?\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0115.wav", "input_sha256": "425f92be59171877dec281c6414f9619dfde45f63ec7c9755b417a80bd6f497e", "input_samples": 209600, "input_s": 13.1, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.4682, "act": 0.9979, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so we have a couple of conversion rates here. One trink et is equal to four blink ets, and three blink ets are equal to seven trinkets. We want to find out how many tri nkets are in 5 6 drinkets. Let' s start by looking at the second conversion rate: three blinkets equal seven trinkets. If I divide both sides by three, I get that one blinket equals about two point three trinkets. But wait, let's use the first conversion directly since it might be simpler. One trink et is four blinkets, so four blinkets make one trinket. That means one blink et is one-fourth of a tri nket.Now, back to the other relationship: three blink ets equal seven tri nkets. So if I have three blinkets, that' s seven tri nkets. To find out what one blinket is worth, I can divide seven tri nkets by three blinkets, which gives me about two point three three tri nkets per blinket. But actually, there's an easier way using the first conversion. Since one tri nket is four blink ets, then one blink et is one-fourth of a tri nket. Now, if three blink ets are seven tri nkets, then on