{"id": "q0169", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2235220061, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "A coil of 60 ohms inductive reactance in series with a resistance of 25 ohms is connected to an a-c line of 130 volts. What will be the current through the circuit?\n\nA. 2.5 amp\nB. 0.5 amp\nC. 2.8 amp\nD. 3.0 amp\nE. 1.0 amp\nF. 2.0 amp\nG. 1.5 amp\nH. 4.0 amp\nI. 3.5 amp\nJ. 1.2 amp\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0169.wav", "input_sha256": "40118582d40c337b583cd1369cba354274cbf41755cad11b30fe352f499dfd0c", "input_samples": 400800, "input_s": 25.05, "n_real_chunks": 26, "score": 0.6654, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "This is an RL circuit with a resist ance of 2 5 ohms and inductive reactance of 60 ohms. First, we need to calculate the imp edance using Z equals square root of R squared plus X L squared. So that would be square root of 2 5 squared plus 6 0 squared, which is about 6 5 ohms. Then, current I equals V divided by Z, so it would be 1 30 divided by 6 5, which is approximately 2 amps. The closest option is F, 2 amps.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 25, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 29, "feed_lag_max_ms": 10435, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 151657, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0169_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "307507b501230778e5a8dcbd345798b50dc3b43e5c1270bc76d